<title>USA: Iowa-So Minn hogs actual Monday 100,000 - USDA.</title>
<headline>Iowa-So Minn hogs actual Monday 100,000 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Actual interior Iowa and southern Minnesota hog receipts Monday were 100,000 head, compared with the estimate of 95,000, USDA reported.</p>
<p>Opening trade was not well established.  Early sales Barrows and Gilts $0.50-$1.00 per cwt higher than the midsession Monday.</p>
<p>				  Country		   Plants</p>
<p>US 1-3   46-49% Carcass Base Lean</p>
<p>220-260 lbs	    60.00 -60.50	   61.00 -61.50</p>
<p>few			61.00 -61.50 &amp;	 62.00 -62.50 &amp;</p>
<p>few				 59.50		    60.50</p>
<p>Sows:  steady to 2.00 lower, decline on weights over 500 lbs..</p>
<p>US 1-3 300-450 lbs.  44.00 -45.00	   45.00 -47.00</p>
<p>450-500 lbs.	   45.00 -47.00	   45.00 -47.00</p>
<p>500 lbs. up	    46.00 -48.00	   46.00 -50.00</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
